2.1 The substrate and the 14-mode multiplet

The substrate is the periodic square lattice Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8 with N = 64
sites. The framework constants are

    d = 4,   N = d * 2^d = 64,   L = sqrt(N) = 8,   H = 2^d = 16.

The discrete 5-point Laplacian

    (Delta f)(x_1, x_2) = 4 f(x_1, x_2) - sum_{|e|=1} f(x + e)

has eigenvalues

    lambda(n_1, n_2) = 4 - 2 cos(pi n_1 / 4) - 2 cos(pi n_2 / 4),

with (n_1, n_2) in {0, ..., 7}^2. The self-paired eigenvalue lambda = 4 has
multiplicity 14.

In the standard mode order

    (nu, e, u, d, s, mu, dark, c, tau, b, W, Z, H, t),

the mode coordinates are

    nu:(0,4),   e:(4,0),   u:(1,3),    d:(1,5),
    s:(3,1),    mu:(3,7),  dark:(5,7), c:(7,3),
    tau:(7,5),  b:(5,1),   W:(2,2),    Z:(2,6),
    H:(6,2),    t:(6,6).

The modes decompose under D4 into three orbits

    O_0 = {nu, e},
    O_1 = {u, d, s, mu, dark, c, tau, b},
    O_2 = {W, Z, H, t},

of sizes (2, 8, 4) with stabilizer orders (4, 1, 2).

