3. THE SELECTION PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

Theorem 3.1 (Zero State Selection). The vacuum is the state of the 14-mode
multiplet that minimizes the total squared expectation value of the 19
vacuum-native observables:

    s = argmin_{||s||=1} ||M^T s||^2.   (Eq. 3.1)

Since M has rank 13 and nullity 1 (Thm. 2.2), the unique minimizer is the
nullvector of M^T, i.e. the zero state.

The theorem is proved constructively in Sections 4 and 5 by two independent
routes.

