5. THE ENTROPY-WELL ROUTE
================================================================================

Theorem 5.1 (Entropy-well selection of the zero state). Identifying the
dimensional deviation epsilon with the observable magnitude ||M^T s||, the
entropy well of Eq. 2.1 becomes

    S(s)/S_0 = 1 - gamma*||M^T s||^2 + O(||M^T s||^4),   (Eq. 5.1)

and maximizing S(s) is equivalent to M^T s = 0.

Proof. We proceed in three steps: bridge identification, substitution, and
extremization.

Step 1: Bridge identification. The dimensional deviation epsilon = D - 4 is a
scalar on the multiplet. The physical properties of epsilon are:

    (a) D4-invariant: the emergent dimension is the same for all 14 modes;
    (b) non-negative: epsilon measures a deviation magnitude;
    (c) vanishes exactly at the vacuum: D = 4 at equilibrium.

The observable magnitude ||M^T s|| has all three properties:

    (a) D4-invariant: M is built from D4-invariant observables (support, IPR,
        N/4, etc. are D4-orbit-constant);
    (b) non-negative by definition of the Euclidean norm;
    (c) vanishes exactly at the vacuum: ||M^T s|| = 0 iff M^T s = 0 iff s is
        the zero state.

The identification is therefore unique up to a positive multiplicative
constant. Normalizing S(0)/S_0 = 1 fixes the constant to unity:

    epsilon = ||M^T s||.   (Eq. 5.2)

Step 2: Substitution. Substituting Eq. 5.2 into Eq. 2.1:

    S(s)/S_0 = 1 - gamma*||M^T s||^2 + O(||M^T s||^4),

which is Eq. 5.1.

Step 3: Extremization. Since gamma > 0 and ||M^T s||^2 >= 0 with equality iff
M^T s = 0, the entropy functional S(s) is maximized exactly on the nullspace of
M^T. By HCSM-22 Thm. 4, the nullspace is 1-dimensional, and the unique
maximizer is the zero state.  QED

Corollary 5.2 (Vacuum entropy maximum). S(s_zero)/S_0 = 1 exactly. For any
other state s != +-s_zero, S(s)/S_0 < 1.

Proof. Immediate from Thm. 5.1 and the positivity of gamma.  QED

Remark 5.3 (Why the entropy well is not a coincidence). The entropy well of
HCSM-54 is derived from the DME stability coefficient gamma, which comes from
the self-dual modular structure of the square torus. The state-dependent
extension S(s)/S_0 = 1 - gamma*||M^T s||^2 is not a new postulate; it is the
natural state-dependent completion of the dimensional form. The bridge
epsilon = ||M^T s|| is the physical statement that the observable magnitude
and the dimensional deviation are the same quantity.

