7. UNIQUENESS OF THE MAXIMIZER
================================================================================

Theorem 7.1 (Uniqueness). The minimizer of ||M^T s||^2 subject to ||s|| = 1
is unique up to sign.

Proof. The minimizer is the normalized nullvector of M^T, equivalently the
eigenvector of M M^T with eigenvalue 0. Since rank(M) = 13 (Thm. 2.2), the
matrix M M^T has a single zero eigenvalue with multiplicity 1. The associated
eigenspace is 1-dimensional. The normalized basis is unique up to sign.  QED

Corollary 7.2 (Vacuum uniqueness). The vacuum state of the 14-mode multiplet
is unique up to the physical sign convention +-1.

