10. FALSIFICATION TESTS
================================================================================

  (1) Vacuum with nonzero observable. A confirmed vacuum with <O_a> != 0 for
      some vacuum-native observable O_a would falsify Thm. 4.1.

  (2) Non-maximizer selection. A confirmed vacuum state s with S(s)/S_0 < 1
      while another state s' has S(s')/S_0 > S(s)/S_0 would falsify Thm. 5.1.

  (3) Entropy-well deviation. A measured S(epsilon)/S_0 != 1 - gamma*epsilon^2
      + O(epsilon^4) would falsify Eq. 5.1 and, by extension, the
      identification epsilon = ||M^T s||.

  (4) Rank-nullity violation. A measured rank(M) != 13 or nullity(M^T) != 1
      would falsify Thm. 7.1. (This test requires the full 19-column M.)

  (5) Route disagreement. A demonstration that the Landauer route and the
      entropy-well route select different states would falsify Thm. 6.1.

