DC.description: HCSM-22 constructs the zero state s as the unique nullvector
    of the 14x19 measurement matrix M, but explicitly does not select s. This
    sub-paper supplies the selection rule. We prove that the vacuum is the
    state of the 14-mode multiplet that minimizes ||M^T s||^2 subject to
    ||s|| = 1. Two independent derivations are given: the Landauer route
    (processor T at the deterministic Landauer bound) and the entropy-well
    route (S(s)/S_0 = 1 - gamma*||M^T s||^2, maximized exactly when
    M^T s = 0). The two routes are dual descriptions of the same minimum-
    information principle. The uniqueness of the maximizer is established
    from rank(M) = 13 and nullity(M^T) = 1 (HCSM-22, Thm. 4). Item 2.1 of the
    HCSM derivation list (Zero State Selection Principle) is closed. All
    numerical claims are verified at machine precision.
